# 4. CUSTOMER-APPROVED BUSINESS MODEL

Individual application:

Student → School preliminary review → School recommendation and one-time forwarding → City independent review → Committee official decision.

### School supplementation

The School reviewer may request a correction while holding authorized preliminary review authority.

The Student responds within the original application.

The School reviewer checks the response and reassesses the relevant declarations.

### City supplementation

The authorized City reviewer may request a correction during City review.

The Student responds within the same original application, through the allowed City supplementation scope.

The City reviewer checks and reassesses.

The School's previous judgments remain historical records and must not be silently overwritten.

### Committee

The Committee receives the accumulated dossier and results for official decision-making.

Do not introduce a Committee supplementation workflow unless it is already explicitly supported and approved.

### Collective

Collective TT01–TT04 applications go directly to City.

Preserve the existing Collective supplementation workflow.

Where practical, share presentation components but not inappropriate Individual criterion logic.

