# 21. SCHOOL/CITY AUTHORITY BOUNDARIES

This is mandatory.

## School

May request supplementation only when permitted for the relevant School Review Unit, stage and application.

## City

May request supplementation only when permitted for City review.

City uses the authorized shared queue.

No mandatory individual assignment.

## Student

May view and respond only to authorized requests concerning their own application.

## Committee

May view authorized history and evidence, but does not inherit School/City supplementation mutation rights.

## Admin

General administrative access must not automatically grant substantive review authority.

### Critical negative tests

- School reviewer requests correction for another School Review Unit.
- Student accesses another Student's supplement request.
- School reviewer edits a City-issued request.
- City reviewer overwrites a School judgment.
- Reviewer changes a forwarded School dossier outside allowed supplementation rules.
- Student edits unrelated submitted data during supplementation.

All must be denied when unauthorized.

