# 37. DEFINITION OF DONE

LEAN-3 is complete only when:

- A reviewer can request supplementation directly from the relevant declaration or supported canonical review scope.
- The system automatically carries the correct context into the request editor.
- The reviewer does not have to reselect unnecessary fields.
- The Student sees the request inside the original dossier.
- The Student can provide explanation and permitted evidence.
- Unrelated submitted content remains protected.
- Historical evidence and judgment records remain traceable.
- The Student can submit the correction through actual supported backend operations.
- The correct School or City reviewer receives the returned supplement.
- Reassessment uses the LEAN-2 direct human Pass/Fail interaction.
- New evidence is not automatically approved.
- Derived criterion results remain accurate.
- No unapproved supplementation deadline is introduced.
- No new ResolutionCase or assignment process is created.
- Demo and Real Mode remain isolated.
- Mobile and desktop layouts are usable.
- Authorization and audit tests pass.
- Any unavailable Real Mode integration is explicitly marked unverified or blocked.

Do not report full PASS based only on a visually attractive Demo UI.

